  "summary": "The 2024 NHL Entry Draft was the league’s 62nd annual draft, held June 28–29 at Sphere in Paradise, Nevada. It set the rights to eligible players and marked the first time the San Jose Sharks held the first overall pick.\n\nSan Jose selected Macklin Celebrini first. The Chicago Blackhawks chose Artyom Levshunov second, and the Anaheim Ducks selected Beckett Sennecke third. The Sharks and Blackhawks won the two draft lotteries on May 7, but the draft order did not change, the first time that had happened since 2010.\n\nUnder an April agreement, draft rights held by the deactivated Arizona Coyotes transferred to the new Utah Hockey Club. Teams also traded numerous picks before and during the draft, reshaping selections across the first two rounds.",
